# Android APK releases

Distribution repo: [rf4burns/Kurier-Android-Installer](https://github.com/rf4burns/Kurier-Android-Installer)

When Gordon asks to **release** the Android app / APK:

1. Gather client-facing changelog bullets (required). Use what he gives; otherwise take the current version notes from `lib/app/release_notes.dart`. Placeholders like `Build 1.0.6.` are not allowed.
2. From this repo root, bump and build:
   `powershell -File tool/build_android.ps1 -Notes "bullet one. | bullet two."`
   Use `-NoBump` only if he asks to rebuild the same version.
3. Copy `build/app/outputs/flutter-apk/app-release.apk` to `Kurier-{x.y.z}.apk` (version from `pubspec.yaml`, no `+build`).
4. Publish a GitHub Release on `rf4burns/Kurier-Android-Installer` (tag `v{x.y.z}`, title `Kurier Android {x.y.z}`). Attach that APK. Put the changelog in the release body as markdown bullets.
5. Do not commit APK binaries into this Flutter repo or into the installer git tree. Releases hold the APKs.
6. Do not rewrite the installer README unless he asks. Source of truth stays this tree; do not commit in Brozantine-Kurier-Android.

Example:

```powershell
gh release create "v1.0.9" "Kurier-1.0.9.apk" --repo rf4burns/Kurier-Android-Installer --title "Kurier Android 1.0.9" --notes "## Changelog`n- First bullet.`n- Second bullet."
```
